# Confirm that the rocMLIR-side and upstream-MLIR-side ROCm-aware artefacts
# never have ROCm runtime libraries (libamdhip64, libhiprtc, libamd_comgr)
# nor ROCm's monolithic libLLVM.so on their dynamic-link `NEEDED` set.
#
# Direct linkage to any of those would defeat the entire delay-load design:
# the runtime loader pulls them in at startup via DT_NEEDED, runs their
# static constructors, and re-introduces the multi-LLVM `cl::opt` collision
# we worked around with `dlmopen(LM_ID_NEWLM, ...)`.
#
# We deliberately scan binaries we ship (rocmlir-driver / -opt / -gen,
# xmir-runner, rocmlir-tuning-driver, mlir-runner) and the ROCm-aware
# shared libraries that compose them. `libMLIRRockOps.so` may legally
# carry `libMLIRRocmRuntimeLoader.so` (our static delay-load helper); it
# must NOT carry `libamdhip64`.
#
# Notes:
#   - This test parses `readelf -d` output in pure shell + grep.
#   - We accept missing artefacts (e.g. mlir_rocm_runtime is only built
#     when `MLIR_ENABLE_ROCM_RUNNER=ON`); we only check what exists.
#   - The check looks for the bare SONAME prefixes; a future ROCm major
#     version (e.g. `libamdhip64.so.8`) would still match.

# REQUIRES: linux

# RUN: %S/check_no_rocm_neededs.sh %rocmlir_shlib_dir %rocmlir_tools_dir
